CosmicTiger build target selection
=================================

@cosmictiger_variant_count@ physics configurations:
  Without SPH: 2 integrators x 3 gravity methods x @cosmictiger_variant_order_count@ orders = @cosmictiger_nosph_variant_count@
  With gravity and SPH:    leapfrog x 3 gravity methods x @cosmictiger_variant_order_count@ orders = @cosmictiger_sph_variant_count@

  Without gravity: cosmictiger_leapfrog_sph (one order-independent SPH target)

SPH supports leapfrog with all three gravity methods. Hierarchical stepping
lacks hydro integration and requires SPH disabled. This restriction means the SPH
choice does not double every combination.

Gravity-enabled target format: cosmictiger_<integrator>_<gravity>[_sph]_<order>
Include _sph to enable SPH; omit it for collisionless targets.

Choose a target family below and replace <order> with one of:
  @cosmictiger_variant_order_help@

@cosmictiger_variant_family_help@
Gravity names:
  none      SPH only: cosmictiger_leapfrog_sph, without gravitational forces
  fmm       Global FMM
  pmmm_pp   PMMM with direct particle-particle near interactions
  pmmm_fmm  PMMM with FMM near interactions

Examples (run from this build directory):
  make -j12 cosmictiger_leapfrog_sph
  make -j12 cosmictiger_leapfrog_pmmm_pp_7
  make -j12 cosmictiger_leapfrog_fmm_sph_7
  make -j12 cosmictiger_leapfrog_pmmm_fmm_sph_7
  make -j12 cosmictiger_hierarchical_pmmm_fmm_5

Build only the target you need. Selecting another named target does not require
reconfiguring and reuses the shared core library and previously built objects.

Position storage: @COSMICTIGER_POSITION_TYPE@ (default: fixed32).
Each target builds one executable. Select fixed32 or fixed64 when configuring:
  cmake -S @PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR@ -B . -DCOSMICTIGER_POSITION_TYPE=fixed64
Target and executable names stay the same. Rebuild after changing this option.
The runtime compute.positionType option, if supplied, must match the build.

Select the SPH-only default with -DCOSMICTIGER_GRAVITY_METHOD=none,
-DCOSMICTIGER_WITH_SPH=ON, and -DCOSMICTIGER_TIME_INTEGRATOR=leapfrog.
FMM order does not apply to this target. Cosmology and FFTW support remain shared.

Configured default: @cosmictiger_default_variant@
  make cosmictiger    Builds the configured default executable.
  make                Builds that default executable and enabled tests/tools.
                      It does not build all physics configurations.

Build type: @CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE@    CUDA: @COSMICTIGER_WITH_CUDA@    Tests: @BUILD_TESTING@
These settings apply to the whole build directory, outside the physics matrix.

  make cosmictiger_help    Shows this guide without compiling.
  make help               Lists CMake's available build targets.
  cmake --build . --target cosmictiger_help    Equivalent help with any generator.
